src/vendor/geoarrow/geoarrow.h and geoarrow.c are the output of
upstream's CMake bundler (GEOARROW_BUNDLE=ON) with
GEOARROW_NAMESPACE=Zugeo, GEOARROW_USE_FAST_FLOAT=OFF (fast_float is
C++) and GEOARROW_USE_RYU=ON; the C++ geoarrow.hpp is left out.
src/vendor/geoarrow/ryu/ is upstream's src/geoarrow/ryu unchanged.
src/vendor/geoarrow/geoarrow_type.h is not upstream's: a one-line header
tools/derive-vendor writes, because ryu/common.h includes that name and
the bundle folds it into geoarrow.h. tools/derive-vendor is the
derivation; tools/verify-vendor re-runs it and fails on any difference.

